{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775351072-KgyTOfNNQYpUydTvsvRT","role":"assistant","created":1775351075,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me first understand the problem:\n1. I need to find the compound annual growth rate (CAGR) for expenditure transfers to the trust fund for Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance\n2. From FY 1947 to the fiscal year during which the Korean War started\n3. The Korean War started in 1950, but I need to figure out which fiscal year\n\nLet me first check when the Korean War started in terms of US fiscal year. The Korean War started on June 25, 1950. The US fiscal year starts on October 1, so:\n- FY 1950 would be October 1, 1949 to September 30, 1950\n- FY 1951 would be October 1, 1950 to September 30, 1951\n\nSince the Korean War started on June 25, 1950, that would be in FY 1950. So I need to find the trust fund transfers for FY 1947 and FY 1950.\n\nNow let me look at the resources to find the Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance trust fund transfers.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_c8f1e1dcd8564afb88f1f3b4","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1953_02_page_25.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
